1
00:00:04,257 --> 00:00:05,927
♪

2
00:00:07,637 --> 00:00:09,187
( Kirito grunting )

3
00:00:11,807 --> 00:00:14,267
Alice: LET GO OF MY HAND
THIS INSTANT, SINNER!

4
00:00:14,267 --> 00:00:17,317
I WOULD RATHER DIE
THAN BE SAVED BY YOU.

5
00:00:17,317 --> 00:00:19,607
I WILL NOT BEAR
THE DISGRACE OF IT! ( grunts )

6
00:00:19,607 --> 00:00:22,237
Kirito: HEY! STOP!

7
00:00:22,237 --> 00:00:24,407
DON’T, YOU IDIOT!

8
00:00:24,407 --> 00:00:26,157
WHAT’S SUICIDE GONNA DO?

9
00:00:26,157 --> 00:00:28,207
NOTHING, THAT’S WHAT,
SO SUCK IT UP,

10
00:00:28,207 --> 00:00:31,377
ACT LIKE A KNIGHT,
AND QUIT BEIN’ AN IDIOT!

11
00:00:31,377 --> 00:00:34,287
Alice: HOW DARE YOU,
A COMMON CRIMINAL, INSULT ME?!

12
00:00:34,287 --> 00:00:35,667
I DEMAND AN APOLOGY.

13
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:37,837
Kirito: OH, SHUT UP!
I CALLED YOU AN IDIOT,

14
00:00:37,837 --> 00:00:39,797
’CAUSE YOU’RE ACTIN’
LIKE AN IDIOT, IDIOT!

15
00:00:39,797 --> 00:00:43,007
LISTEN! IF I LET GO
AND YOU DIE, THEN WHAT?

16
00:00:43,007 --> 00:00:44,597
EUGEO’S STILL IN THE CATHEDRAL,

17
00:00:44,597 --> 00:00:47,137
AND HE’S ON HIS WAY
UP TO THE PONTIFEX,

18
00:00:47,137 --> 00:00:49,517
AND IT’S YOUR JOB TO STOP HIM,
YOU IDIOT!

19
00:00:49,517 --> 00:00:51,397
( Alice grumbles )

20
00:00:51,397 --> 00:00:53,647
Kirito: INSTEAD OF CHECKIN’ OUT,
AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT

21
00:00:53,647 --> 00:00:56,357
SHOULD BE THINKIN’
HOW TO GET BACK IN, BUT NOT YOU.

22
00:00:56,357 --> 00:00:58,857
YOU’RE SO DUMB,
YOU FORGOT YOUR PRIORITIES,

23
00:00:58,857 --> 00:01:01,277
AND THAT’S WHY YOU’RE AN IDIOT!

24
00:01:01,277 --> 00:01:03,697
Alice: LOOK HERE.
I WON’T ALLOW A ROGUE LIKE YOU

25
00:01:03,697 --> 00:01:05,577
TO INSULT ME ANY FURTHER.

26
00:01:07,577 --> 00:01:11,617
THAT SAID, YOUR WORDS HAVE
A CERTAIN LOGIC TO THEM.

27
00:01:11,617 --> 00:01:15,377
HOWEVER, DEATH IS MORE TOLERABLE
THAN BEING SAVED OUT OF PITY,

28
00:01:15,377 --> 00:01:17,707
AND LETTING ME FALL
WOULD BENEFIT YOUR CAUSE,

29
00:01:17,707 --> 00:01:19,257
SO WHY DON’T YOU?

30
00:01:19,257 --> 00:01:22,757
EXPLAIN WHY I MUST ACCEPT
THIS SITUATION!

31
00:01:22,757 --> 00:01:23,677
Kirito: I’LL TRY.

32
00:01:24,757 --> 00:01:26,387
( singing in Japanese )

33
00:01:26,387 --> 00:01:29,137
♪

34
00:01:57,627 --> 00:02:00,087
♪ PROUD OF MYSELF ♪

35
00:02:07,427 --> 00:02:09,097
♪

36
00:02:59,427 --> 00:03:01,557
Kirito: EUGEO AND ME,

37
00:03:01,557 --> 00:03:03,847
WE DIDN’T BREAK IN AND
GET THIS FAR UP THE CATHEDRAL

38
00:03:03,847 --> 00:03:06,607
JUST TO DESTROY
THE AXIOM CHURCH.

39
00:03:06,607 --> 00:03:10,187
WE KNOW THE DARK TERRITORY’S
GONNA INVADE THE HUMAN EMPIRE,

40
00:03:10,187 --> 00:03:12,027
AND WE WANNA PROTECT IT,
SAME AS YOU.

41
00:03:17,447 --> 00:03:20,327
YOU’RE ONE OF THE MOST POWERFUL
INTEGRITY KNIGHTS AROUND,

42
00:03:20,327 --> 00:03:23,707
AND, IF I LET YOU DIE,
WE LOSE A VALUABLE ALLY.

43
00:03:23,707 --> 00:03:25,747
- ( Alice gasps )
- Kirito: WE CAN’T AFFORD THAT.

44
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:27,417
Alice: WHY SHOULD
I BELIEVE YOU?

45
00:03:27,417 --> 00:03:29,337
YOU VIOLATED
THE GRAVEST TABOO OF ALL,

46
00:03:29,337 --> 00:03:31,337
SPILLING THE BLOOD
OF A FELLOW HUMAN

47
00:03:31,337 --> 00:03:33,257
AND CUTTING THEM DOWN.

48
00:03:33,257 --> 00:03:35,087
Kirito: THAT’S TRUE.

49
00:03:35,087 --> 00:03:39,057
BUT THE AXIOM CHURCH
AND THE TABOO INDEX ARE WRONG.

50
00:03:39,057 --> 00:03:43,097
EUGEO AND I HAD A GOOD REASON
TO ATTACK RAIOS AND HUMBERT.

51
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:45,187
THE LAWS LET
UPPER-CLASS NOBLES LIKE THEM

52
00:03:45,187 --> 00:03:47,227
DO WHATEVER THEY WANT
TO INNOCENT PEOPLE.

53
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:50,607
THOSE BASTARDS
WERE GONNA RAPE RONIE AND TIESE

54
00:03:50,607 --> 00:03:53,277
AND GET AWAY WITH IT.
DO YOU THINK THAT’S RIGHT?

55
00:03:53,277 --> 00:03:55,607
DO YOU THINK THAT’S FAIR?!

56
00:03:55,607 --> 00:03:57,657
WELL, IS IT?

57
00:03:57,657 --> 00:03:59,827
ANSWER ME! IS IT RIGHT?!

58
00:04:02,657 --> 00:04:04,747
Alice: THE LAW IS THE LAW.

59
00:04:04,747 --> 00:04:07,327
A CRIME IS A CRIME.

60
00:04:07,327 --> 00:04:09,587
IF THE PEOPLE
ARE ALLOWED TO DECIDE

61
00:04:09,587 --> 00:04:12,587
WHAT IS RIGHT AND WRONG
ACCORDING TO THEIR NEEDS,

62
00:04:12,587 --> 00:04:15,547
HOW WILL WE MAINTAIN ORDER
IN THE LAND?

63
00:04:15,547 --> 00:04:17,007
Kirito: YEAH, WELL,

64
00:04:17,007 --> 00:04:19,347
ADMINISTRATOR CAME UP
WITH ALL THE LAWS,

65
00:04:19,347 --> 00:04:22,427
SO WHO DECIDES
IF SHE’S RIGHT OR WRONG?

66
00:04:22,427 --> 00:04:24,137
YOUR GOD?

67
00:04:24,137 --> 00:04:26,097
IF I’M SUCH A SINNER,
THEN HOW COME

68
00:04:26,097 --> 00:04:28,727
I HAVEN’T BEEN FRIED
BY A BOLT OF LIGHTNING BY NOW?

69
00:04:28,727 --> 00:04:32,567
Alice: SIMPLE.
IT IS THE WILL OF STACIA,

70
00:04:32,567 --> 00:04:34,567
AND WE KNIGHTS ENFORCE HER WILL.

71
00:04:34,567 --> 00:04:36,157
WE ARE HER DIVINE SERVANTS.

72
00:04:36,157 --> 00:04:38,317
Kirito: ALL YOU KNIGHTS
ENFORCE ARE LIES,

73
00:04:38,317 --> 00:04:40,577
AND ME AND EUGEO
CAME HERE TO PROVE IT!

74
00:04:40,577 --> 00:04:43,787
IF WE DEFEAT ADMINISTRATOR,
WE’LL END HER TYRANNY.

75
00:04:43,787 --> 00:04:45,707
WE’RE NOT THE BAD GUYS!

76
00:04:45,707 --> 00:04:48,077
IF WE WERE,
I’D HAVE LET YOU FALL.

77
00:04:49,417 --> 00:04:51,297
( wall creaking )

78
00:04:51,297 --> 00:04:52,297
( gasps )

79
00:04:53,837 --> 00:04:55,377
IT’S COMIN’ LOOSE!

80
00:04:55,377 --> 00:04:58,587
STICK YOUR SWORD IN THE WALL,
OR WE DIE!

81
00:04:58,587 --> 00:05:00,757
( groaning )

82
00:05:02,887 --> 00:05:04,847
WHAT ARE YOU WAITING FOR? DO IT!

83
00:05:04,847 --> 00:05:07,227
MINE’S ABOUT TO COME OUT! HURRY!

84
00:05:10,687 --> 00:05:12,227
( gasps )

85
00:05:18,857 --> 00:05:20,867
( Alice grunting )

86
00:05:20,867 --> 00:05:22,277
( Kirito gasps )

87
00:05:22,277 --> 00:05:23,447
( yelps )

88
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:28,617
( sword stabs )

89
00:05:30,127 --> 00:05:32,537
Alice: I DID NOT
SAVE YOU, SINNER.

90
00:05:32,537 --> 00:05:34,547
I RETURNED THE FAVOR, IS ALL.

91
00:05:34,547 --> 00:05:38,837
BESIDES, OUR DUEL
HAS YET TO BE DECIDED.

92
00:05:38,837 --> 00:05:40,587
Kirito: IF WE SURVIVE.

93
00:05:40,587 --> 00:05:43,257
OH, WELL.
AT LEAST WE’RE EVEN NOW.

94
00:05:44,717 --> 00:05:46,387
I GOT AN IDEA,
IF YOU WANNA HEAR.

95
00:05:48,057 --> 00:05:50,017
WE CAN’T HANG HERE ALL DAY.

96
00:05:50,017 --> 00:05:51,477
OUR ARMS’LL GET TIRED.

97
00:05:51,477 --> 00:05:54,687
BUT IF WE WORK TOGETHER,
WE CAN FIND A WAY BACK IN.

98
00:05:54,687 --> 00:05:58,067
SO, LIKE, WHAT DO YOU SAY
WE CALL A TRUCE ’TIL THEN?

99
00:05:58,067 --> 00:05:59,737
- Alice: A TRUCE?
- Kirito: YEAH.

100
00:05:59,737 --> 00:06:02,527
WE CAN’T BREAK THE WALL,
SO WE’LL HAVE TO CLIMB.

101
00:06:02,527 --> 00:06:04,827
IT’LL BE EASIER
IF WE HELP EACH OTHER.

102
00:06:04,827 --> 00:06:06,617
Alice: YOU SAY,
"HELP EACH OTHER."

103
00:06:06,617 --> 00:06:08,537
HOW DO YOU PROPOSE WE DO THAT?

104
00:06:08,537 --> 00:06:10,417
Kirito: IF ONE OF US
STARTS TO FALL,

105
00:06:10,417 --> 00:06:11,957
THE OTHER STOPS ’EM. THAT’S ALL.

106
00:06:11,957 --> 00:06:15,047
IF WE HAD A ROPE, WE COULD
USE IT AS A SAFETY LINE.

107
00:06:15,047 --> 00:06:16,757
I DIDN’T BRING ONE, THOUGH.

108
00:06:16,757 --> 00:06:22,427
Alice: I HATE TO ADMIT IT,
BUT THAT DOES SOUND LOGICAL.

109
00:06:22,427 --> 00:06:23,097
VERY WELL.

110
00:06:25,007 --> 00:06:28,727
HOWEVER, THE MOMENT
WE SET FOOT INSIDE AGAIN,

111
00:06:28,727 --> 00:06:30,387
I WILL CUT YOU DOWN.

112
00:06:30,387 --> 00:06:34,057
TRUCE OR NO,
DO NOT FORGET THAT.

113
00:06:34,057 --> 00:06:35,357
Kirito: I’LL TRY NOT TO.

114
00:06:35,357 --> 00:06:39,187
Alice: NOW, THEN,
YOU SAID WE NEEDED ROPE.

115
00:06:39,187 --> 00:06:42,277
SYSTEM CALL. FORM OBJECT.
CHANGE SHAPE.

116
00:06:47,117 --> 00:06:49,997
Kirito: W-WAS THAT
THE MATTER CONVERSION ART?!

117
00:06:49,997 --> 00:06:51,827
Alice: DID YOU
NOT HEAR WHAT I SAID?

118
00:06:51,827 --> 00:06:54,457
I CHANGED
THE SHAPE OF AN OBJECT.

119
00:06:54,457 --> 00:06:56,917
ONLY THE PONTIFEX
CAN USE THE FORMAL ARTS

120
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:59,337
TO CHANGE AN OBJECT’S
PROPERTIES, YOU DOLT.

121
00:07:00,797 --> 00:07:02,427
Kirito: SORRY, MA’AM.

122
00:07:02,427 --> 00:07:04,257
♪

123
00:07:11,557 --> 00:07:12,437
( sighs )

124
00:07:23,737 --> 00:07:24,867
( gasps )

125
00:07:24,867 --> 00:07:26,657
( swallows )

126
00:07:26,657 --> 00:07:29,747
HEY, UM, I JUST THOUGHT
OF SOMETHING ELSE.

127
00:07:29,747 --> 00:07:31,497
Alice: WHAT IS IT?

128
00:07:31,497 --> 00:07:33,787
Kirito: IT’S ABOUT
THAT DRAGON OF YOURS.

129
00:07:33,787 --> 00:07:36,747
CAN’T YOU, LIKE,
SUMMON IT TO COME GET US?

130
00:07:36,747 --> 00:07:38,417
Alice: MINE CANNOT FLY FURTHER

131
00:07:38,417 --> 00:07:41,047
THAN THE LANDING PLATFORMS
ON THE 30th FLOOR.

132
00:07:41,047 --> 00:07:44,757
NO DRAGON CAN. EVEN MY UNCL--

133
00:07:44,757 --> 00:07:47,467
PARDON. EVEN THE COMMANDER’S
IS NOT ALLOWED.

134
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:50,467
THE UPPER FLOORS ARE OFF LIMITS.

135
00:07:50,467 --> 00:07:52,637
EVEN THE BIRDS STAY AWAY.

136
00:07:52,637 --> 00:07:55,437
THE PONTIFEX HERSELF MADE IT SO.

137
00:07:55,437 --> 00:07:57,107
SHE CAST A FORMAL ART,

138
00:07:57,107 --> 00:07:59,687
ONE SO ADVANCED,
I DO NOT EVEN KNOW IT.

139
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:02,187
Kirito: OH, WELL.

140
00:08:02,187 --> 00:08:04,777
I GUESS THAT LEAVES US
WITH THREE OPTIONS, THEN.

141
00:08:04,777 --> 00:08:08,947
GO UP OR DOWN
OR BUST THROUGH THE WALL AGAIN.

142
00:08:08,947 --> 00:08:10,737
Alice: THE THIRD OPTION IS OUT.

143
00:08:10,737 --> 00:08:14,577
THE CATHEDRAL WALLS ARE ENDOWED
WITH NEARLY INFINITE LIFE,

144
00:08:14,577 --> 00:08:17,127
AND, AS YOU SAW,
THEY REGENERATE QUICKLY.

145
00:08:17,127 --> 00:08:18,957
Kirito: PERFECT.

146
00:08:18,957 --> 00:08:22,007
ALL RIGHT,
I’M THINKING WE SHOULD CLIMB.

147
00:08:22,007 --> 00:08:24,047
DO YOU KNOW IF THERE’S ANYWHERE
UP TOP WHERE WE CAN GET IN?

148
00:08:26,087 --> 00:08:27,887
Alice: THERE IS.

149
00:08:27,887 --> 00:08:31,717
THE MORNING STAR LOOKOUT
IS ON THE 95th FLOOR.

150
00:08:31,717 --> 00:08:33,927
THERE ARE NO WALLS,
JUST PILLARS.

151
00:08:33,927 --> 00:08:37,847
IF WE CAN CLIMB UP THAT FAR,
WE CAN EASILY GET BACK IN.

152
00:08:37,847 --> 00:08:42,567
THAT SAID, IF WE MANAGE
TO SURVIVE THE CLIMB AND GET IN,

153
00:08:42,567 --> 00:08:45,857
OUR TRUCE IS OFF,
AND I WILL SLAY YOU.

154
00:08:45,857 --> 00:08:48,367
Kirito: I KNOW.
I DIDN’T FORGET ABOUT OUR DEAL.

155
00:08:48,367 --> 00:08:52,237
( sighs ) SO ARE YOU OKAY
WITH CLIMBING UP, OR WHAT?

156
00:08:52,237 --> 00:08:55,537
Alice: YES. GOING UP
IS MORE PRACTICAL THAN DOWN,

157
00:08:55,537 --> 00:08:58,537
BUT HOW DO YOU PLAN
ON SCALING A SHEER WALL?

158
00:08:58,537 --> 00:08:59,747
IT WON’T BE EASY.

159
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:01,087
Kirito: SYSTEM CALL.

160
00:09:01,087 --> 00:09:03,087
GENERATE METALLIC ELEMENT.

161
00:09:03,087 --> 00:09:04,717
WEDGE SHAPE!

162
00:09:04,717 --> 00:09:07,047
♪

163
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:08,967
( grunting )

164
00:09:18,267 --> 00:09:20,857
Alice: IS THAT
SAFE TO STAND ON?

165
00:09:20,857 --> 00:09:23,107
Kirito: SEEMS TO BE, FOR NOW.

166
00:09:24,187 --> 00:09:25,857
SYSTEM CALL.

167
00:09:25,857 --> 00:09:27,947
GENERATE METALLIC ELEMENT.

168
00:09:27,947 --> 00:09:28,697
( grunts )

169
00:09:33,077 --> 00:09:35,497
YOU KNOW, I THINK THIS’LL WORK.

170
00:09:35,497 --> 00:09:37,997
WELL? DON’T JUST HANG THERE.
DO WHAT I DID.

171
00:09:39,077 --> 00:09:40,827
Alice: I CANNOT.

172
00:09:40,827 --> 00:09:41,837
Kirito: HUH?

173
00:09:41,837 --> 00:09:43,997
WH-WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

174
00:09:43,997 --> 00:09:46,047
Alice: I SAID I CANNOT!

175
00:09:46,047 --> 00:09:48,967
Kirito: YEAH, I HEARD THAT,
BUT WHAT DO YOU MEAN, YOU CAN’T?

176
00:09:48,967 --> 00:09:52,887
IF I CAN MAKE A WEDGE, YOU CAN.
AND YOU’RE SO STRONG,

177
00:09:52,887 --> 00:09:54,717
YOU SHOULDN’T HAVE
ANY PROBLEM HOISTING--

178
00:09:54,717 --> 00:09:56,847
Alice: THAT IS NOT WHAT I MEANT!

179
00:09:56,847 --> 00:10:00,397
I HAVE NEVER BEEN IN A SITUATION
LIKE THIS BEFORE TODAY.

180
00:10:00,397 --> 00:10:02,977
A-AT THE RISK OF SOUNDING WEAK,

181
00:10:02,977 --> 00:10:06,147
IT IS ALL I CAN MANAGE
TO JUST HANG ON.

182
00:10:06,147 --> 00:10:09,397
I CANNOT CLIMB UP
ONTO SUCH A SLENDER STEP.

183
00:10:09,397 --> 00:10:12,657
Kirito: NO WORRIES. HOW ’BOUT
IF I PULL YOU UP TO THE BAR?

184
00:10:12,657 --> 00:10:14,157
WOULD THAT WORK
FOR YOU INSTEAD?

185
00:10:14,157 --> 00:10:17,077
Alice: I WOULD APPRECIATE IT.

186
00:10:17,077 --> 00:10:19,787
Kirito: OKAY. FIRST I’M
GONNA TAKE UP THE SLACK.

187
00:10:19,787 --> 00:10:21,077
HERE GOES!

188
00:10:21,077 --> 00:10:23,337
♪

189
00:10:28,717 --> 00:10:30,337
I’M READY. GO ON,
AND PULL YOUR SWORD OUT.

190
00:10:33,677 --> 00:10:35,137
( grunts )

191
00:10:36,597 --> 00:10:38,677
( Alice gasps )

192
00:10:38,677 --> 00:10:40,347
♪

193
00:10:50,067 --> 00:10:52,817
( shuddering )

194
00:10:52,817 --> 00:10:54,567
Kirito: GRAB THE WALL
TO BALANCE!

195
00:10:56,487 --> 00:11:00,537
ALL RIGHT, I’M GONNA CLIMB UP
A LITTLE HIGHER NOW.

196
00:11:00,537 --> 00:11:01,617
I’LL LET YOU KNOW
WHEN I’M READY.

197
00:11:02,957 --> 00:11:03,997
Alice: PLEASE BE CAREFUL.

198
00:11:03,997 --> 00:11:05,247
Kirito: ALWAYS.

199
00:11:14,297 --> 00:11:16,047
( waves crashing )

200
00:11:22,887 --> 00:11:23,557
( Rinko gasps )

201
00:11:27,727 --> 00:11:29,857
- HEY, ASUNA.
- Asuna: HUH?

202
00:11:29,857 --> 00:11:31,487
Rinko: HOW’S YOUR FISH?

203
00:11:31,487 --> 00:11:33,487
I BET THEY CAUGHT IT RIGHT
OFF THE SIDE OF THE TURTLE.

204
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:37,277
Asuna: YEAH, MAYBE THEY DID.

205
00:11:37,277 --> 00:11:39,037
OR MAYBE THEY BROUGHT IT.

206
00:11:39,037 --> 00:11:39,697
Rinko: WHO?

207
00:11:42,287 --> 00:11:45,167
HMM. I DOUBT IT.

208
00:11:45,167 --> 00:11:47,457
DOESN’T LOOK
LIKE A FISHING BOAT.

209
00:11:47,457 --> 00:11:49,377
IT’S GOT WAY TOO MANY ANTENNAE.

210
00:11:49,377 --> 00:11:51,257
Asuna: IS IT A BATTLESHIP?

211
00:11:51,257 --> 00:11:53,087
Nakanishi: NO. IT’S JAPANESE.

212
00:11:53,087 --> 00:11:56,137
WE DON’T HAVE BATTLESHIPS
IN SERVICE ANYMORE.

213
00:11:56,137 --> 00:11:59,097
MS. YUUKI, DR. KOJIRO, MORNING.

214
00:11:59,097 --> 00:12:00,677
Asuna: GOOD MORNING.

215
00:12:00,677 --> 00:12:02,557
Rinko: GOOD MORNING,
MR. NAKANISHI.

216
00:12:02,557 --> 00:12:05,807
IF THAT’S NOT A WARSHIP,
IS IT S.D.F.?

217
00:12:05,807 --> 00:12:07,607
Nakanishi: M.S.D.F.,

218
00:12:07,607 --> 00:12:10,277
AND "ESCORT SHIP"
IS THE OFFICIAL DESIGNATION.

219
00:12:10,277 --> 00:12:14,357
THE ONE OUT THERE
IS THE "DD119 ASAHI."

220
00:12:14,357 --> 00:12:17,157
SHE’S A FIVE-TON,
GENERAL-PURPOSE VESSEL.

221
00:12:17,157 --> 00:12:18,737
SHE’S ONE OF TWO ESCORT SHIPS
IN SERVICE.

222
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:20,117
( women giggling )

223
00:12:20,117 --> 00:12:21,577
Nakanishi: HER SISTER SHIP
IS THE "SHIRANUI"...

224
00:12:21,577 --> 00:12:23,407
Asuna: HEY, IT LOOKS
LIKE IT’S MOVING AWAY NOW.

225
00:12:23,407 --> 00:12:25,667
Nakanishi: ...SECOND GENERATION
OF THEIR CLASS. EH?

226
00:12:28,037 --> 00:12:28,917
( sighs )

227
00:12:28,917 --> 00:12:30,047
PARDON ME.

228
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:36,047
LIEUTENANT COLONEL KIKUOKA?

229
00:12:36,047 --> 00:12:39,257
I JUST SAW THE "ASAHI"
CHANGING COURSE TO THE WEST.

230
00:12:39,257 --> 00:12:41,137
WASN’T SHE
SUPPOSED TO STAY WITH US

231
00:12:41,137 --> 00:12:43,677
UNTIL 1200,
DAY AFTER TOMORROW?

232
00:12:44,767 --> 00:12:46,137
YES, SIR. RIGHT AWAY.

233
00:12:48,607 --> 00:12:50,227
EXCUSE ME, LADIES.
SOMETHING’S COME UP.

234
00:12:53,987 --> 00:12:57,357
Rinko: HMM. IT MUST BE
SOMETHING IMPORTANT.

235
00:12:57,357 --> 00:12:58,277
Asuna: YEAH.

236
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:08,997
( sighs )

237
00:13:11,997 --> 00:13:12,877
( Kirito grunting )

238
00:13:21,007 --> 00:13:22,387
SYSTEM CALL.

239
00:13:22,387 --> 00:13:24,887
GENERATE METALLIC ELEMENT.

240
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:26,017
Alice: THE LIGHT.

241
00:13:29,097 --> 00:13:31,307
( Kirito sighs )

242
00:13:31,307 --> 00:13:32,687
Alice: GENERATING CONTAINERS

243
00:13:32,687 --> 00:13:35,857
USES UP A SIGNIFICANT AMOUNT
OF SACRED POWER,

244
00:13:35,857 --> 00:13:38,107
AND ONCE SOLUS SETS,

245
00:13:38,107 --> 00:13:41,027
WE’LL BE LUCKY IF WE
CAN CREATE ONE BAR AN HOUR.

246
00:13:41,027 --> 00:13:42,327
( Kirito sighs )

247
00:13:42,327 --> 00:13:45,117
Alice: HOW HIGH UP
DO YOU THINK WE ARE NOW?

248
00:13:45,117 --> 00:13:46,577
Kirito: UM...

249
00:13:46,577 --> 00:13:49,457
I THINK WE’RE ALREADY PAST
THE 85th FLOOR.

250
00:13:49,457 --> 00:13:53,167
Alice: THE 95th FLOOR
IS STILL QUITE A LONG WAY OFF.

251
00:13:53,167 --> 00:13:56,417
Kirito: YEAH, AND CLIMBING’S
GONNA BE EVEN MORE DANGEROUS

252
00:13:56,417 --> 00:13:57,877
ONCE IT’S TOO DARK TO SEE.

253
00:14:00,387 --> 00:14:02,297
EH? HEY, CHECK IT OUT!

254
00:14:02,297 --> 00:14:03,847
THERE’S SOMETHING ON THAT LEDGE.

255
00:14:03,847 --> 00:14:06,347
♪

256
00:14:06,347 --> 00:14:09,057
Alice: THEY LOOK
LIKE STATUES FROM HERE,

257
00:14:09,057 --> 00:14:11,437
WHICH IS ODD.
NO ONE BELOW CAN SEE THEM.

258
00:14:11,437 --> 00:14:14,857
Kirito: OH, WELL. THEIR LOSS,
BUT MAYBE WE CAN REST ON ’EM.

259
00:14:14,857 --> 00:14:17,187
THEY LOOK LIKE
THEY’RE ABOUT SIX METER--

260
00:14:17,187 --> 00:14:18,567
SIX MELS AWAY.

261
00:14:18,567 --> 00:14:21,607
WE’RE GONNA NEED TWO MORE BARS.

262
00:14:21,607 --> 00:14:23,577
Alice: YOU ONLY NEED TWO,
YOU SAY?

263
00:14:25,037 --> 00:14:26,657
VERY WELL, THEN.

264
00:14:26,657 --> 00:14:30,037
I WAS SAVING IT
FOR AN EMERGENCY.

265
00:14:30,037 --> 00:14:31,827
IT APPEARS THIS WOULD BE ONE.

266
00:14:33,207 --> 00:14:36,247
FORM OBJECT. WEDGE SHAPE.

267
00:14:38,377 --> 00:14:40,467
HERE. USE THESE.

268
00:14:40,467 --> 00:14:43,137
Kirito: THANKS! I OWE YOU.

269
00:14:47,217 --> 00:14:49,057
( grunting )

270
00:14:53,647 --> 00:14:55,477
GET READY. I’M PULLIN’ YOU UP.

271
00:14:55,477 --> 00:14:56,397
Alice: RIGHT.

272
00:14:58,227 --> 00:15:00,447
Kirito: YOU GOOD?

273
00:15:00,447 --> 00:15:01,987
Alice: I’M FINE.

274
00:15:01,987 --> 00:15:02,987
Kirito: OH.

275
00:15:02,987 --> 00:15:05,197
♪

276
00:15:05,197 --> 00:15:06,117
( Alice gasps )

277
00:15:07,987 --> 00:15:09,907
NO.

278
00:15:09,907 --> 00:15:11,657
Kirito: OH, MY GOD.

279
00:15:11,657 --> 00:15:14,077
THAT SURE IS ONE UGLY STATUE.

280
00:15:14,077 --> 00:15:15,037
( gasps )

281
00:15:18,417 --> 00:15:19,917
( creature growls )

282
00:15:19,917 --> 00:15:21,257
Alice: IT’S FROM
THE DARK TERRITORY!

283
00:15:21,257 --> 00:15:22,717
( creature roars )

284
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:26,007
Kirito: ALICE!

285
00:15:26,007 --> 00:15:29,217
♪

286
00:15:29,217 --> 00:15:29,967
ALICE!

287
00:15:31,307 --> 00:15:32,227
( creature 2 roars )

288
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:35,557
( creature 1 roars )

289
00:15:35,557 --> 00:15:36,647
( Kirito gasps )

290
00:15:48,157 --> 00:15:49,487
( grunts )

291
00:15:49,487 --> 00:15:51,117
( creature 1 roars )

292
00:15:52,577 --> 00:15:54,117
Kirito: DRAW YOUR SWORD! HURRY!

293
00:15:54,117 --> 00:15:56,327
THERE’S TWO MORE COMIN’!

294
00:15:56,327 --> 00:15:57,377
( creature 2 roars )

295
00:15:57,377 --> 00:15:59,917
( Alice gasping )

296
00:15:59,917 --> 00:16:01,377
Kirito: ALICE!

297
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:03,047
( creatures growling )

298
00:16:06,137 --> 00:16:09,097
Kirito: WE’RE SCREWED
IF THEY ATTACK AT ONCE.

299
00:16:09,097 --> 00:16:11,137
WHAT THE HELL’S UP WITH HER?!

300
00:16:13,177 --> 00:16:14,227
( sighs )

301
00:16:14,227 --> 00:16:15,687
ALICE!

302
00:16:17,687 --> 00:16:19,147
- ALICE!
- ( Alice gasps )

303
00:16:19,147 --> 00:16:20,727
Kirito: HANG ON
AS TIGHT AS YOU CAN!

304
00:16:20,727 --> 00:16:23,277
Alice: N-NOW, JUST A MOMENT.

305
00:16:23,277 --> 00:16:26,067
Kirito: I’LL APOLOGIZE LATER,
IF WE SURVIVE!

306
00:16:26,067 --> 00:16:27,407
GET READY!

307
00:16:27,407 --> 00:16:30,367
ONE, TWO...

308
00:16:30,367 --> 00:16:31,657
- THREE!
- ( Alice whimpers )

309
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:34,367
( Kirito yells )

310
00:16:34,367 --> 00:16:38,127
( Alice screams )

311
00:16:44,297 --> 00:16:46,007
( grunts )

312
00:16:46,007 --> 00:16:48,177
( yells )

313
00:16:48,177 --> 00:16:50,177
( Kirito yells )

314
00:16:50,177 --> 00:16:51,967
( groans )

315
00:16:51,967 --> 00:16:54,477
Alice: WHAT WERE YOU THINKING,
YOU IDIOT?!

316
00:16:54,477 --> 00:16:56,977
HAVE YOU LOST YOUR MIND?!

317
00:16:56,977 --> 00:16:59,187
Kirito: I DIDN’T HAVE
ANY OTHER CHOICE.

318
00:16:59,187 --> 00:17:01,107
I HAD TO ACT.

319
00:17:01,107 --> 00:17:02,317
WE’LL TALK LATER.
HERE THEY COME!

320
00:17:02,317 --> 00:17:03,567
( Alice gasps )

321
00:17:03,567 --> 00:17:05,987
( creatures growling )

322
00:17:05,987 --> 00:17:07,487
♪

323
00:17:09,487 --> 00:17:10,157
( Kirito gasps )

324
00:17:14,077 --> 00:17:15,117
Alice: THERE IS NO DOUBT.

325
00:17:16,707 --> 00:17:19,877
( gasps ) BUT WHY ARE THEY HERE?

326
00:17:19,877 --> 00:17:22,707
Kirito: I WAS WONDERING
WHEN YOU’D SNAP OUT OF IT.

327
00:17:22,707 --> 00:17:24,667
DO YOU KNOW
WHAT THESE MONSTERS ARE?

328
00:17:24,667 --> 00:17:27,837
Alice: YES, I DO, INDEED.

329
00:17:27,837 --> 00:17:31,257
THEY ARE FAMILIARS
FROM THE DARK TERRITORY,

330
00:17:31,257 --> 00:17:33,557
CONJURED FROM LUMPS
OF CORRUPT SOIL

331
00:17:33,557 --> 00:17:36,307
BY SORCERERS
WHO PRACTICE THE DARK ARTS.

332
00:17:36,307 --> 00:17:39,397
SUCH DISGUSTING THINGS.

333
00:17:39,397 --> 00:17:41,397
WE CALL THESE CREATURES MINIONS.

334
00:17:41,397 --> 00:17:43,357
Kirito: THAT FIGURES.

335
00:17:43,357 --> 00:17:44,777
BUT WHY ARE THEY HERE?

336
00:17:44,777 --> 00:17:46,647
THIS IS THE HOLIEST PLACE
IN THE LAND,

337
00:17:46,647 --> 00:17:48,147
AND THEY’RE
JUST HANGING OUT ON IT.

338
00:17:48,147 --> 00:17:49,857
Alice: I’D LIKE
TO KNOW WHY AS WELL!

339
00:17:51,197 --> 00:17:52,697
THEY SHOULD NOT BE HERE

340
00:17:52,697 --> 00:17:56,077
FOULING THE VERY SYMBOL
OF ALL THAT IS GOOD.

341
00:17:56,077 --> 00:17:58,407
I CANNOT BELIEVE
THEY ESCAPED THE NOTICE

342
00:17:58,407 --> 00:17:59,707
OF THE INTEGRITY KNIGHTS

343
00:17:59,707 --> 00:18:01,627
TO ROOST
ON THE CENTRAL CATHEDRAL,

344
00:18:01,627 --> 00:18:04,167
WHERE EVEN THE BIRDS
CANNOT LAND.

345
00:18:04,167 --> 00:18:06,047
IT’S UNREAL.

346
00:18:06,047 --> 00:18:07,717
Kirito: YEAH, WELL,
NOT IF ADMINISTRATOR

347
00:18:07,717 --> 00:18:09,677
WANTED THESE SUCKERS HERE.

348
00:18:09,677 --> 00:18:12,637
I DON’T KNOW WHY SHE WOULD,
BUT IT’S POSSIBLE.

349
00:18:12,637 --> 00:18:15,597
AT THIS POINT,
IT WOULDN’T SURPRISE ME.

350
00:18:15,597 --> 00:18:20,307
WATCH IT! THE OTHER TWO
ARE COMING AROUND AGAIN!

351
00:18:20,307 --> 00:18:23,147
Alice: I KNOW. THIS IS
NOT MY FIRST TIME IN BATTLE.

352
00:18:23,147 --> 00:18:24,437
( minions growling )

353
00:18:24,437 --> 00:18:26,687
♪

354
00:18:37,367 --> 00:18:38,827
Alice: DO YOU NEED ASSISTANCE
WITH THAT ONE?

355
00:18:40,287 --> 00:18:41,417
Kirito: NOPE! I CAN HANDLE HIM!

356
00:18:50,467 --> 00:18:52,217
( yells )

357
00:18:58,727 --> 00:18:59,977
( Alice gasps )

358
00:19:02,807 --> 00:19:04,517
( Kirito sighs ) YOU OKAY?

359
00:19:04,517 --> 00:19:05,937
Alice: I AM.

360
00:19:05,937 --> 00:19:08,397
I WAS JUST THINKING
HOW STRANGE YOUR MOVES ARE.

361
00:19:08,397 --> 00:19:11,277
IF YOU PERFORMED THEM
AT THE MIDSUMMER FESTIVAL,

362
00:19:11,277 --> 00:19:13,277
YOU WOULD ATTRACT
QUITE AN AUDIENCE.

363
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:15,827
Kirito:
THANKS FOR THE COMPLIMENT.

364
00:19:15,827 --> 00:19:19,537
HANG ON. HAVE YOU BEEN TO
THE MIDSUMMER FESTIVAL BEFORE?

365
00:19:19,537 --> 00:19:21,867
I THOUGHT
IT WAS ONLY FOR COMMONERS.

366
00:19:21,867 --> 00:19:24,667
EVEN KIDS FROM THE UPPER-CLASS
FAMILIES STAYED AWAY,

367
00:19:24,667 --> 00:19:27,497
AT LEAST THE ONES I WAS
GOING TO THE ACADEMY WITH.

368
00:19:27,497 --> 00:19:29,167
Alice: DO NOT MENTION ME

369
00:19:29,167 --> 00:19:31,627
IN THE SAME BREATH
AS THOSE SO-CALLED NOBLES.

370
00:19:31,627 --> 00:19:33,637
I’VE SEEN IT. I--

371
00:19:33,637 --> 00:19:36,297
I’VE BEEN...

372
00:19:36,297 --> 00:19:37,967
Kirito: A-ALICE?

373
00:19:37,967 --> 00:19:41,767
Alice: NO.
I HAVE ONLY HEARD OF IT.

374
00:19:41,767 --> 00:19:45,147
ONE OF THE PRIESTS
MUST HAVE TOLD ME OF IT.

375
00:19:45,147 --> 00:19:46,727
WE INTEGRITY KNIGHTS,

376
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:49,817
WE ARE PROHIBITED FROM MINGLING
WITH THE TOWNSFOLK,

377
00:19:49,817 --> 00:19:51,737
EXCEPT IN THE LINE OF DUTY.

378
00:19:53,397 --> 00:19:54,567
Kirito: WHAT?

379
00:19:54,567 --> 00:19:56,657
Alice: MINION BLOOD
CARRIES DISEASE.

380
00:19:56,657 --> 00:19:59,617
YOU SHOULD WIPE IT OFF.

381
00:19:59,617 --> 00:20:01,117
Kirito: HUH? OH.

382
00:20:01,117 --> 00:20:02,867
( Alice gasps )
NO, NOT LIKE THAT!

383
00:20:02,867 --> 00:20:05,037
( Kirito gasps )

384
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:08,627
Alice: HONESTLY! COULD A MAN
BE ANY MORE THOUGHTLESS?

385
00:20:08,627 --> 00:20:11,877
ARE YOU SO UNCOUTH, YOU DO
NOT EVEN HAVE A HANDKERCHIEF?

386
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:14,007
Kirito: N-NO, I DON’T.

387
00:20:14,007 --> 00:20:16,427
Alice: AS I THOUGHT. USE MINE.

388
00:20:16,427 --> 00:20:17,137
Kirito: UH...

389
00:20:18,547 --> 00:20:20,637
THANKS. I APPRECIATE IT.

390
00:20:20,637 --> 00:20:21,387
Alice: UH...

391
00:20:21,387 --> 00:20:23,347
( scoffs )

392
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:25,557
I WOULD LIKE IT
WASHED AND RETURNED

393
00:20:25,557 --> 00:20:27,267
BEFORE I SLAY YOU.

394
00:20:29,397 --> 00:20:30,357
( Kirito chuckles )

395
00:20:30,357 --> 00:20:32,277
♪

396
00:20:35,527 --> 00:20:37,197
Eugeo: NOW THAT I THINK OF IT,

397
00:20:37,197 --> 00:20:39,987
EVER SINCE I MET KIRITO
TWO YEARS AGO,

398
00:20:39,987 --> 00:20:42,577
HE’S ALWAYS BEEN WITH ME.

399
00:20:42,577 --> 00:20:45,207
I’VE FORGOTTEN
WHAT IT’S LIKE TO BE ALONE.

400
00:20:47,787 --> 00:20:50,127
I HOPE HE’S OKAY.

401
00:20:50,127 --> 00:20:52,297
KNOWING HIM, I’M SURE HE IS.

402
00:20:52,297 --> 00:20:53,797
HE’S PROBABLY
CLIMBING THE TOWER,

403
00:20:53,797 --> 00:20:55,507
LOOKING FOR A WAY IN

404
00:20:55,507 --> 00:20:57,257
ALONG WITH ALICE.

405
00:21:05,517 --> 00:21:06,977
THE 90th FLOOR.

406
00:21:10,727 --> 00:21:12,727
AN INTEGRITY KNIGHT
IS IN THERE.

407
00:21:15,277 --> 00:21:16,197
HERE GOES.

408
00:21:20,527 --> 00:21:22,197
( door grinding )

409
00:21:34,757 --> 00:21:37,717
IT’S A GIANT BATH.

410
00:21:37,717 --> 00:21:39,387
- ( water splashes )
- ( gasps )

411
00:21:43,557 --> 00:21:44,677
Knight: EASY, KID.

412
00:21:44,677 --> 00:21:47,017
I NEED TO STRETCH
BEFORE WE START.

413
00:21:49,597 --> 00:21:53,147
I JUST GOT BACK
FROM PATROLLING THE BORDERLANDS.

414
00:21:53,147 --> 00:21:57,197
RIDING THAT DRAGON NONSTOP
SURE DOES A NUMBER ON THE BODY.

415
00:21:59,777 --> 00:22:00,907
( Eugeo gasps )

416
00:22:02,697 --> 00:22:03,617
( Knight sighs )

417
00:22:03,617 --> 00:22:05,407
( chuckles )

418
00:22:05,407 --> 00:22:09,497
Singer: ♪ OH, EVERYTHING
TURNS TO ASH, TO ASH ♪

419
00:22:09,497 --> 00:22:11,167
( singing in Japanese )

420
00:22:19,047 --> 00:22:22,507
♪ AND EVERYTHING
TURNS TO DUST, TO DUST ♪

421
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:24,177
( singing in Japanese )

422
00:22:31,937 --> 00:22:33,897
♪ FORGET-ME-NOT ♪
